<!--
  A one-way road that leads nowhere next to a network of roads, as the one-way streets at the Zócalo in Mexico City
  lead only to streets that are no roads of the graph. One country, AAA, from 1°W to 2°E and 1°S to 1°N:

    road 1, along the equator from 0° to 1°E: a two-way secondary (60 km/h) with a junction every 0.04° from 0.02°E
            to 0.98°E, each with a tooth: a secondary road 0.02° (2.2 km) south. 52 nodes of the graph with its ends.
    road 2: a one-way secondary from road 1's junction at 0.5°E north to 0.2°N, where it ends.

  The origin, (0.15°N, 0.505°E), is 0.56 km from road 2 and 16.7 km from road 1. From road 2 only its end is
  reachable, fewer than 50 nodes, so the origin snaps to road 1, at 0.505°E: 16.7 km at 30 km/h, 0.556 h at the
  wheel, 0.667 h of travel. Road 1 takes 0.222 h of travel per 0.1°, so the ring of 2 h holds (0°, 0.8°E), 0.295°
  on, at 1.323 h, and not (0°, 0.6°E), at 0.878 h. Snapped to road 2, the origin would reach nothing after 0.133 h.

         0.2°N                    r2
                                  ^
                                  |    * the origin
           0° 0-+---+---+---+-...-+-...-+---+---+-1°E   road 1
                |   |   |   |     |     |   |   |       its teeth
       0.02°S
-->
